            <div xml:id="d764">

                <pb facs="1040" n="1030" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1030"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119P.W./10–145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kennan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-10-01">October 1,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received October 1—11:50 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3415. Press September 30 published despatch datelined Changchun September 29
                    reporting that partial withdrawal of Soviet troops from Manchuria had begun
                    several days ago. Withdrawal of main forces, stated despatch, will begin in
                    second half of October and withdrawal of all Soviet forces will be complete by
                    end of November. Withdrawal is being directed by Marshal Malinovski and Chinese
                    Command has been informed.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 3415, repeated Chungking 173.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennan</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
